{"type":"process","design":"","title":"Follow-the-sun incident escalation workflow","lead":"Global engineering handoffs keep critical platform incidents moving continuously until resolved.","items":[{"title":"Automated alert capture","text":"Cloud Monitoring and Dataplex quality rules detect pipeline anomalies or SLA breaches and trigger PagerDuty alerts with diagnostic metadata. Teams isolate broken ingestion paths immediately.","icon":"alert-circle"},{"title":"Immediate bridge activation","text":"On-call L1 and L2 engineers open a live conference bridge day or night to coordinate triage and execute standardized runbooks. Incident commanders assign specific investigative tasks.","icon":"phone"},{"title":"Follow-the-sun engineering","text":"L3 architects across North America, Costa Rica, the UK, and India pass active diagnostics across time zones for uninterrupted remediation. Handoff briefs document all attempted fixes.","icon":"globe-circle"},{"title":"Root-cause closure","text":"Engineers verify data parity, close the incident, and update Terraform modules and monitoring thresholds to prevent repeat occurrences. Root-cause analyses outline preventive safeguards.","icon":"shield-check"}],"notes":"66degrees operates a global follow-the-sun delivery and support network spanning the United States, Canada, Costa Rica, the UK, and India. When an alert fires, expert engineers open a conference bridge immediately and work the issue continuously across time zones until full resolution and root-cause closure.

