{"type":"diagram","design":"S66_LAYER_STACK","title":"Multi-region backup and point-in-time recovery","lead":"Cross-region Cloud Storage buckets and Persistent Disk snapshots protect ePHI against corruption.","layers":[{"label":"Transaction log capture","items":["SQL Server Agent schedules routine full, differential, and log dumps.","Automated transaction log backups run continuously to minimize data loss.","Encrypted backup streams protect all clinical payload data during transit."],"icon":"analytics"},{"label":"Multi-region object storage","items":["Dual-region Cloud Storage buckets provide immediate cross-zone resilience.","Cross-region synchronous bucket replication ensures immediate offsite redundancy.","CMEK key binding enforces full customer control over data encryption keys."],"icon":"hard drive"},{"label":"Ransomware immutability controls","items":["Bucket Lock retention policies enforce strict compliance retention terms.","WORM object immutability preserves clinical backups against modification.","Deletion and overwrite block safeguards archives from operational errors."],"icon":"scale"},{"label":"Point-in-time recovery tier","items":["35-day point-in-time recovery enables granular transactional restorations.","Encrypted Persistent Disk snapshots secure full-volume machine states offsite.","Isolated DR project restore guarantees clean recovery testing environments."],"icon":"time"}],"notes":"High availability replication does not replace immutable backups against logical corruption or ransomware. This four-tier backup architecture streams automated SQL Server transaction log backups into dual-region Cloud Storage buckets protected by Bucket Lock WORM retention policies and CMEK, enabling point-in-time recovery across a 35-day window alongside Persistent Disk snapshots.

