{"type":"process","title":"Delivery risks and proactive technical mitigations","lead":"Structured technical and governance controls neutralize schema drift, metric disputes, and query cost spikes early.","items":[{"title":"Source schema drift and metric disputes","text":"Unannounced POS or ERP schema changes break pipelines while merchandising teams debate net margin formulas.","points":["Enforce automated schema validation gates in landing zones","Route non-conforming payloads into dead-letter quarantine tables","Lock canonical LookML KPI logic in week-two workshops"]},{"title":"Unpredictable BigQuery compute cost spikes","text":"Unconstrained ad-hoc queries from store and merchandising analysts trigger sudden cloud compute overruns.","points":["Configure BigQuery Editions slot reservations with hard caps","Mandate table partitioning on transaction date and SKU","Route BI dashboard traffic through cached Looker aggregates"]},{"title":"Analyst adoption lag post-cutover","text":"Merchandising and inventory teams revert to manual spreadsheet extracts instead of self-service Looker explores.","points":["Embed retail domain stewards directly inside sprint reviews","Run role-based Looker champion enablement before production cutover","Decommission legacy manual CSV extracts after parallel validation"]}],"notes":"We proactively mitigate four primary delivery risks before they impact schedule or budget. Automated schema validation and week-two KPI workshops prevent pipeline breaks and metric disputes, while BigQuery slot reservations and Looker champion training protect cloud budgets and drive analyst adoption.

